# RXPart erosion spline prototype

Open `/Game/Study/RX_PCGTest/RXTestMap`. `Mapsetting` selects Erosion1 by
default. RXPart is a Level Instance with fixed PLA architecture and an editor
preview. Gameplay loads only the selected environment's Blueprint asynchronously.
Lighting remains Erosion1 Day, Erosion2 Twilight, Erosion3 Evening.
Runtime uses Blueprint and UE 5.6 native PCG only. These Python scripts are
editor authoring and verification tools; there is no project C++ change.

## Edit generation areas

Open RXPart for editing. Each erosion has its own `BP_SplineRegion_ErosionN`
class, seven Include splines and five Exclude splines, attached to its own
`ErosionLayout`. Erosion1 is red, Erosion2 green, Erosion3 blue. Selected curves
are yellow. Exclusions take precedence over inclusions. No box or brush is needed.

Select a region and move its ordinary spline points in the viewport. Regions are
open ribbons. For a wall, rotate the region so local XY follows the wall and local
Z points through the surface; the PCG projects in both local normal directions.
Pillars use the same approach on each desired face. Add another spline for another
face or disconnected patch. The target PLA must provide query collision.
Duplicate the matching erosion's region actor and attach it to ErosionLayout;
another erosion's splines do not participate. Each Level Instance uses its own
layout, target and attached regions, including after translation and rotation.

| Region parameter | Meaning |
|---|---|
| RegionMode | Include or Exclude; an exclusion always wins |
| Width | Half width on each side of the curve, in cm |
| EdgeFalloff | 0 gives constant density; 1 fades toward the edge |
| ProjectionDepth | Half depth in front of/behind the ribbon, in cm |
| MaxCount | This Include spline's upper limit; 0 disables its generation |
| Density | This Include spline's density, 0..1; 0 disables generation |
| PackingGap | Added clearance on each mesh bound in cm; 0 packs closest |
| PackingBoundsScale | Bounds used for pruning only; lower packs closer |
| ActualCount | Read-only final count after exclusions and cross-spline pruning |

Keep ProjectionDepth shallow enough to avoid reaching the back of a wall.
The point scales are set by the Construction Script from Width and ProjectionDepth;
edit curve positions and these parameters rather than point scales. Curves persist
through Blueprint compilation and editor reload. Press `Rebuild Preview` on the
selected spline or ErosionLayout after a change. It rebuilds the selected erosion
only in that Level Instance and updates ActualCount for all its regions. Exclude
and inactive-erosion counts become 0. Generation settings are disabled for Exclude
regions. EditorPreview_RXPart's existing `Refresh Part Preview` still works.

## Edit appearance

Select ErosionLayout. Each Erosion1/2/3 category exposes the same 14 controls.
Identifiers and categories are English; tooltips are Korean. SurfaceTarget is the
shared explicit reference to the local Main PLA.

| Parameter suffix | Purpose |
|---|---|
| Meshes / MeshWeights | Mesh choices and corresponding relative weights |
| Spacing | Candidate sampling spacing in cm; lower costs more |
| ScatterSeed | Repeatable randomized placement |
| RotationMin / RotationMax | Local rotation range in degrees |
| SizeWeights | Relative Small/Medium/Large proportions in XYZ |
| SizeMin / SizeMax | Uniform scale range for Small/Medium/Large in XYZ |
| AttachmentDepth | Offset along the hit surface normal, in cm |
| ClusterSize | Spatial extent of coherent density variation, in cm |
| ClusterContrast | Separation of dense centers and sparse edges |
| MaterialOverride | First material slot override |
| CandidateBudget | Total post-projection budget, equally reserved per Include |

Keep Meshes and MeshWeights the same length with a positive total weight.
Keep minimums below maximums, size weights nonnegative with a positive total,
and spacing/scales positive. MaxCount cannot force points into excluded space;
small areas, low density or large meshes/gaps can reduce the actual count below
200. The saved three prototype presets generate 286, 286 and 266 instances.
World-space cluster noise can produce different counts after moving/rotating a
Level Instance; tune its spline settings when a particular patch needs more.

Candidates jitter before projection, and use coherent density plus random
survival, producing irregular groups with thinning edges. Native size-aware
Self Pruning uses the selected mesh's bounds after final rotation/scale. Large
meshes pack first, medium meshes fill remaining space, and small meshes fill gaps.
PackingGap expands the bounds by the same cm value at every scale.
PackingBoundsScale scales the bounds about their actual centre before clearance,
preserving off-centre pivots. Start with Gap=0 and BoundsScale=1 for contact;
lower BoundsScale gradually for closer packing. Values below 1 can allow actual
mesh penetration. Mesh scale remains controlled by SizeMin/SizeMax. This is a
bounds-based overlap check; it does not perform triangle-level mesh collision.
CandidateBudget caps noise, selection and pruning cost after projection; Spacing
still affects the preceding sampling and ray-query cost.

The cone and chamfered block remain test meshes. Replace Meshes with the intended
barnacle assets to obtain their silhouette; the reference image's hollow geometry
is not part of this procedural placement prototype.

## Replacement and verification

All 36 former include/exclude box actors and their six Blueprint classes were
removed. The three former PCG graphs, three runtime wrappers, three obsolete
option enums and empty probe graph were also removed: 16 legacy assets total.
The four internal GenerationBounds boxes in the preview/runtime Blueprints were
also replaced with hidden, non-colliding two-point PCGAnchor splines. These only
provide the primitive bounds required by native PCG registration and do not define
generation areas. Their former root transforms and non-partitioned setting are
preserved; sampling is unbounded and uses the explicitly scoped region splines.
Architecture, lighting, detailed meshes and materials remain.
ErosionLayout was reduced from 205 to 43 data variables (162 removed), plus one
internal BP dispatcher for editor refresh requests (44 variable descriptions).

Verification scripts use the existing local editor bridge on port 55561:

```powershell
uv run python scripts/rx_pcg_test/open_verified_level.py RXPart
uv run python scripts/rx_pcg_spline/verify_baseline.py
uv run python scripts/rx_pcg_spline/verify_controls.py
uv run python scripts/rx_pcg_spline/verify_region_controls.py
uv run python scripts/rx_pcg_test/bridge.py python scripts/rx_pcg_spline/select_default.py
uv run python scripts/rx_pcg_test/bridge.py python scripts/rx_pcg_test/save_prototype.py
uv run python scripts/rx_pcg_test/open_verified_level.py RXTestMap
uv run python scripts/rx_pcg_spline/verify_runtime.py
uv run python scripts/rx_pcg_spline/verify_instances.py
uv run python scripts/rx_pcg_spline/verify_assets.py
```

`verify_controls.py` temporarily changes and restores 16 meaningful settings,
including curve shape, width, exclusion mode, density, mesh choices, final
transforms and packing. Runtime checks compare every instance's mesh, material,
position, rotation and scale with its editor preview, selected-only loading and
lighting. Instance checks test a translated/rotated duplicate and remove it.
Asset verification compiles all 12 retained/new Blueprints, checks names/tooltips,
native package dependencies, architecture and absence of old box actors.
`verify_region_controls.py` adds seven per-spline cases, checks actual count sums,
unrelated region counts and all-zero clearing through the BP button. The instance
test also verifies the button leaves the other Level Instance unchanged.

The migration removed the nine Layout Count/ClusterDensity/PackingGap variables
only after checking all native PCG property readers and 12 BP node graphs.
The prior limit 2400 was rounded to 343 per Include spline (7 regions), and prior
density .75/gap 1.5 were copied. Existing curve shapes and region masks were kept.
Layout now has 43 data variables and one BP dispatcher. Each region has nine
custom variables.
There are 59 assets: three additional per-erosion packing workers and one shared
native stats worker. EditorPreview_RXPart remains an editor-only Actor and
registers its refresh callback on its own Layout's PreviewRebuildRequested
dispatcher. The Construction Script unbinds the prior Layout before binding the
current Layout, avoiding duplicate/stale registrations. BoundLayout retains its
value across editor reconstruction and is disabled for manual editing. A temporary
log probe verified one callback after five registrations, no callback from the
previous Layout, and correct routing after restoring the reference; the probe
was removed before saving. Layout never references
the Preview class or its three graph components. The saved-package hard dependency
audit proves each runtime wrapper reaches only its own cluster graph. PIE actor
selection is tested separately; this does not claim other assets are unloaded
from an editor process that already displayed all three previews.

Generation projects and packs each Include independently, then merges points and
prunes overlaps across splines before spawning ISMs and counting ownership.
CandidateBudget is divided by the number of Include splines and rounded down;
disabled Includes keep a reserved share so editing them cannot reallocate another
region's candidates. Budget applies after projection; Spacing also controls the
cost of producing surface candidates. MaxCount is an upper bound rather than a
promise to fill an area. Overlapping Include regions can lose points to each other.

Authoring/migration scripts are ordered operations for an existing prototype;
do not run them as a general regeneration command. In particular, the migration
expects the old wrappers to exist, and is not needed on the finished saved assets.
`audit_legacy_assets.py` inspects references without deleting assets. The separately
reviewed offline removal script accepts only its exact 16 audited files, requires
the editor to be stopped, checks containment and preserves hash-verified backups
in Saved. It is a one-time migration operation.

`baseline.json`, `control_verification.json`, `runtime_verification.json`,
`instance_verification.json`, `asset_verification.json` and `asset_snapshot.json`
record the live checks. `spline_cluster_runtime.png` is an actual PIE capture.
